{
  "id": "mcq-orderby-desc-string",
  "unit": "distinct-and-order",
  "mode": "choice",
  "tier": "hard",
  "title": "Which one fails?",
  "topics": [
    "orderBy"
  ],
  "examObjective": "Applying correct syntax to write DataWeave transformations to coerce, format, order, and filter data",
  "prompt": "Three of these run. **One fails.** Which one?",
  "inputMime": "application/json",
  "outputMime": "application/json",
  "choice": {
    "kind": "which-fails",
    "answer": 0,
    "options": [
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n[\"b\", \"a\", \"c\"] orderBy -$",
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n[{ d: |2024-01-02| }, { d: |2024-01-01| }] orderBy $.d",
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n([\"b\", \"a\", \"c\"] orderBy $)[-1 to 0]",
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n[3, 1, 2] orderBy -$"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [],
  "solution": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n([\"b\", \"a\", \"c\"] orderBy $)[-1 to 0]",
  "explanation": {
    "approach": "Negating the sort key reverses a numeric order, but you cannot negate a String. For Strings, sort ascending and then reverse with `[-1 to 0]`.",
    "snippets": [
      {
        "label": "The one that fails",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n[\"b\", \"a\", \"c\"] orderBy -$",
        "expect": {
          "error": true
        },
        "note": "There is no minus for a String."
      },
      {
        "label": "The fix",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n([\"b\", \"a\", \"c\"] orderBy $)[-1 to 0]",
        "expect": {
          "output": "[ \"c\", \"b\", \"a\" ]"
        },
        "note": "Sort, then reverse."
      },
      {
        "label": "Dates sort chronologically",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\n[{ d: |2024-01-02| }, { d: |2024-01-01| }] orderBy $.d",
        "expect": {
          "output": "[ { \"d\": \"2024-01-01\" }, { \"d\": \"2024-01-02\" } ]"
        },
        "note": "A Date sort key is fine."
      }
    ]
  }
}
